PURPOSE
H7 established that a small shared low-rank inherited manifold can preserve multiple recurring developmental priors,
but insufficient rank can become harmful.

H8 asks:

Can the organism decide when one additional slow structural degree of freedom is worth its permanent resource cost,
and when an unused degree should be pruned?

This connects:

H7
bounded inherited representational capacity

with

S4-S9
resource economics,
causal value-of-information,
and reversible trust.

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- implement a real Yggdrasil micro-genome;
- prove real developmental regimes occupy a low-dimensional linear subspace;
- freeze PCA/Oja/Sanger as the implementation;
- define a biological energy constant;
- authorize unbounded structural growth;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

